     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_kelim_tzfonit_chatzi_etzba",
     "gloss_en": "the one on the north-eastern corner exceeded Moses' [cubit] by half a fingerbreadth"
    }
   ]
  },
  "1": {
   "segId": "Bekhorot.40a.2",
   "sugya": "bekhorot_39b_etzba_sheamru",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_kelim_meila",
     "gloss_en": "why was one large and one small? so that the craftsmen would take by the small and return by the large, that they not come to misuse of consecrated property"
    }
   ]
  },
  "2": {
   "segId": "Bekhorot.40a.3",
   "sugya": "bekhorot_39b_etzba_sheamru",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_stam_kaspa_vezahava",
     "gloss_en": "one -- for silver and gold"
    }
   ]
  },
  "3": {
   "segId": "Bekhorot.40a.4",
   "sugya": "bekhorot_39b_etzba_sheamru",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_rnby_chulya",
     "gloss_en": "Rav Nachman bar Yitzchak, and some say Rav Huna bar Natan: [it is said] for that which we learned: where there is flesh between vertebra and vertebra a full fingerbreadth"
    }
   ]
  },
  "10": {
